AMLET
-----

AMLET (Another Mixed Logit Estimation Tool) is a mixed logit
estimation package, allowing use of real or simulated data.

The behaviour of the software is controlled by means of a driver file,
that indicates the model form and the data to be used.

Installation procedure
----------------------

To compile under Linux:

chmod +x bootstrap
./bootstrap
./configure

AMLET has been tested on Debian 2.4, SuSE 7.3 and SuSE 8.0. It
requires a validated version of C compiler. We currently suggest gcc
2.95, or gcc 3.3.1 or superior.

Optimization of the code
------------------------

The code resulting from the compilation is very sensitive to the used
optimization flags. If you know about your machine and
autoconf/automake principles, please check the configure.in file to
put adequate optimization flags for your architecture.

